2. Meaning of internal use

Internal use means use by an individual for their own activities, or by an
organization's personnel and contractors solely for that organization's
internal activities. An organization may deploy the software on its own
systems, make internal modifications, and provide copies to those personnel
and contractors for that purpose, subject to the notices required below.
Contractors do not receive permission to offer the software itself as a
commercial product or service to customers.

Using the software to assist internal coding, design, research, or other work
is permitted even when that work produces goods or services sold by the user.
The sale of independently created work output is not, by itself, a sale or
commercial distribution of this software.

3. Limits of this additional permission

This additional permission does not grant rights to sell, rent, charge for
access to, or commercially redistribute the covered software or modified
